The first segment of `ruleId` must be one of these category slugs. They are a
closed set: a finding whose `ruleId` starts with anything else is rejected.
Pick the slug that names the vulnerability class, and keep the second segment
free for the control family. The heading above each group is the category the
report will file the finding under; it is not itself a slug.

Prefer the most specific applicable slug. Use a broad slug such as
`improper-authorization`, `improper-input-validation`, `info-disclosure`,
`resource-exhaustion`, `session-lifecycle`, `unsafe-configuration`, or
`weak-crypto` only when no specific slug fits. Classify the root cause, not a
downstream impact. Use the second segment to name the vulnerable control.

- Access Controls: `csrf`, `idor`, `improper-authorization`,
  `privilege-escalation`, `workflow-bypass`
- Auditing and Logging: `insufficient-logging`
- Authentication: `auth-bypass`, `missing-authentication`, `weak-authentication`
- Configuration: `supply-chain-integrity`, `unsafe-configuration`
- Cryptography: `cleartext-transmission`, `key-nonce-reuse`, `weak-crypto`,
  `weak-randomness`
- Data Exposure: `credential-exposure`, `hardcoded-secret`, `info-disclosure`,
  `insecure-file-permissions`, `user-enumeration`
- Data Validation: `code-injection`, `command-injection`, `format-string`,
  `header-injection`, `improper-input-validation`, `insecure-deserialization`,
  `log-injection`, `open-redirect`, `path-traversal`, `prompt-injection`,
  `prototype-pollution`, `request-smuggling`, `sql-injection`, `ssrf`,
  `template-injection`, `unrestricted-file-upload`, `xss`, `xxe`
- Denial of Service: `redos`, `resource-exhaustion`
- Error Reporting: `error-message-disclosure`, `fail-open`
- Session Management: `session-fixation`, `session-lifecycle`
- Timing: `race-condition`, `timing-side-channel`
- Undefined Behavior: `buffer-overflow`, `double-free`, `integer-overflow`,
  `null-dereference`, `out-of-bounds-read`, `out-of-bounds-write`,
  `type-confusion`, `uninitialized-memory`, `use-after-free`
